		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Let&#039;s consider:<br />-table test containing fields id and description.<br />-Table audit containing fields id, timestamp, query<br />-The audit_function:</p><p>CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION audit_function() RETURNS TRIGGER AS $audit$<br />&#160; &#160; BEGIN<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; --<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; -- Create a row audit to reflect the operation performed on test,<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; --<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; IF (TG_TABLE_NAME = &#039;test&#039;) THEN<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; IF (TG_OP = &#039;DELETE&#039;) THEN<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; INSERT INTO audit (stamp,query) VALUES(now(), CONCAT(&#039;DELETE FROM test WHERE id=&#039;,OLD.id,&#039;;&#039;));<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; RETURN OLD;<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; ELSIF (TG_OP = &#039;UPDATE&#039;) THEN<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; INSERT INTO audit (stamp,query) VALUES( now(), CONCAT(&#039;UPDATE test SET id=&#039;, NEW.id, &#039;,description=&#039;, quote_literal(NEW.description)&#039;;&#039;));<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; RETURN NEW;<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; ELSIF (TG_OP = &#039;INSERT&#039;) THEN<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; INSERT INTO audit (stamp,query) VALUES( now(), CONCAT(&#039;INSERT INTO test VALUES(&#039;,NEW.id,&#039;,&#039;,quote_literal(NEW.description),&#039;);&#039;));<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; RETURN NEW;<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; END IF;<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; RETURN NULL; <br />&#160; &#160; END;<br />$audit$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;</p><p>-Trigger<br />CREATE TRIGGER test_audit<br />AFTER INSERT OR UPDATE OR DELETE ON test<br />&#160; &#160; FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE PROCEDURE audit_function();</p><p>If i insert record id=1, description=Here&#039;s the example (INSERT INTO test (id,description) VALUES (1,&#039;Here&#039;&#039;s the example&#039;);)<br />I will get in audit table a record with query=INSERT INTO test (stamp,query) VALUES (yyyymmdd-hhmmss,&#039;Here&#039;s the example&#039;);</p>]]></content>
